                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "Looks good to me.\n\nIs that the only place in the code where this race condition would occur?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Good question - \nIn fan-presence, I can see the first read not working, but that's OK because 1) we already OR in the GPIO presence for the real presence value, and 2) it handles PC signals so as soon as the fans start to spin we'd get the new value. \n\nIn fan-monitor, it doesn't care until either the system is powered on, or if a reboot at runtime, until the 'monitor start delay' has expired which is 30s for us."
                }
            ],
